            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A needle shield remover (30) for a medicament delivery device, which needle shield remover (30) comprises a metal tubular body (200), having a proximal part (A), a distal part (B), and a substantially circular cross-section, the tubular body (200) being arranged with a slot (20) extending from a distal end of the body (200), at least half the length of the body (200), towards a proximal end, such that at least the distal part of the body (200) may flex radially outwards to exert a radially inwardly directed clamping force on a needle shield accommodated by the body (200); wherein the slot (20) is formed as a partial cut-out from a distal end of a wall of a metal tube such that the proximal part (A) of the body (200) is radially rigid and the distal part (B) of the body (200) is radially flexible.</p>
            </abstract>
